# The daily paper run on a server (an example: crontab -e and paste, after editing the path).
# CRON_TZ (cronie, the cron of most Linux distributions) reads the schedule in New York time:
# 17:15, after the 16:00 close and the run's 30-minute margin, daylight saving included.
# Holidays: the run reads the NYSE calendar, finds the last session done and does nothing.
CRON_TZ=America/New_York
15 17 * * 1-5  $HOME/pwb-paper/tradewind-daily.sh

# A cron without CRON_TZ, on a UTC clock: run twice, 21:45 and 22:45 UTC (17:45 / 16:45 New
# York in summer, 16:45 / 17:45 in winter). The first run after the close does the session,
# the other one finds it done; a run before the close works on the previous session (done).
# 45 21,22 * * 1-5  $HOME/pwb-paper/tradewind-daily.sh
